    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="83.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 83.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="83.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gyf he þonn<hi rend="italic">e</hi> swa dyrstig sig, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he hit þriddan syðe wyrde, þolige ealles þæs þe he áge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="83.2" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ gif he þonne swa dyrstig sy, þæt he þridde syðe wyrde, þolige ealles þæs þe he age.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="83.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si quis addat tertio, reus sit omnium quę habebit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="83.2" corresp="#wit-b">And gyf he ðonne swa dyrstig sy þæt he hi ðridde siðe abrece, ðolige ealles ðæs ðe he age.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if he is so presumptuous as to break it a third time, he shall lose all that he possesses.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn er dann so frech ist, dass er es zum dritten Male verletzt, verliere er alles, was er besitzt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if he is then so bold that he violates it a third time, let him lose everything that he possesses.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
